// --- GEOMETRY & SHAPES ---

// A regular equilateral triangle with side length s contains exactly s^2 unit triangles.
// Equiangular Hexagon (120 deg angles): Number of unit triangles = (s1 + s2 + s3)^2 - s1^2 - s3^2 - s5^2.
// Pick's Theorem: Area = I + (B/2) - 1 (I = interior integer points, B = points on boundary).
// Distance between (x1, y1) and (x2, y2): sqrt(pow(x2-x1, 2) + pow(y2-y1, 2)).
// Integer points on segment (x1, y1) to (x2, y2): gcd(abs(x1-x2), abs(y1-y2)) + 1.
// Sum of interior angles of any n-sided polygon: (n - 2) * 180 degrees.
// Number of diagonals in an n-gon: n * (n - 3) / 2.
// Right angle triangles triples like 3-4-5 5-12-13 always have a small number where n (the small number) n^2 + m^2 = (m + 1)^2 if the number is even then its m + 2

// --- NUMBER THEORY ---

// Sum of divisors of N: If N = p1^a * p2^b..., sum = (p1^(a+1)-1)/(p1-1) * (p2^(b+1)-1)/(p2-1)...
// Number of divisors of N: (a + 1) * (b + 1) * ...
// GCD(a, b) * LCM(a, b) = a * b.
// Euler's Totient (phi): Number of integers up to n coprime to n: n * product(1 - 1/p).
// Fast Exponentiation (Binary Exponentiation): Compute (a^b) % m in O(log b).

// --- SERIES & SUMMATIONS ---

// Sum of first N integers: n * (n + 1) / 2.
// Sum of first N odd integers: n^2.
// Sum of first N even integers: n * (n + 1).
// Sum of first N squares: n * (n + 1) * (2n + 1) / 6.
// Sum of first N cubes: (n * (n + 1) / 2)^2.
// Arithmetic Progression (AP): Sum = (n / 2) * (first_term + last_term).
// Geometric Progression (GP): Sum = a * (r^n - 1) / (r - 1).

// --- COMBINATORICS & ALGEBRA ---

// Handshaking Lemma: Total degree of a graph = 2 * number of edges.
// Pigeonhole Principle: If n items are put into m containers (n > m), at least one container has >1 item.
// Stars and Bars: Ways to put n identical items into k distinct bins: C(n + k - 1, k - 1).
// Derangements: Number of ways to shuffle n items so none are in original place: !n = (n-1)(!(n-1) + !(n-2)).
// Quadratic Formula: x = (-b ± sqrt(b^2 - 4ac)) / 2a.

